-- title:
--   A normalized separating functional from the absence of an integer certificate
-- statement:
--   Let $I,J$ be finite, let $A_i,u\in\mathbb Z^J$, and suppose the real cone generated by the $A_i$ is closed. Assume there are no $D\in\mathbb N$ with $D>0$ and coefficients $c_i\in\mathbb N$ satisfying $\sum_i c_i A_i=-Du$. Then there is a real-linear functional $L:\mathbb R^J\to\mathbb R$ with
--   \[
--   L(u)=1,\qquad L(A_i)\ge0\quad(i\in I).
--   \]
--   The integral vectors are viewed in real coordinate space. This is the normalized separation step used to construct states.
